            "text": "{\n  \"study_topic_id\": \"study-4d6dd331abd2f9ce3137\",\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"text\": \"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz (1646–1716) was a German philosopher, mathematician, and polymath whose work ranged across metaphysics, logic, and mathematics. A leading rationalist, he argued that reality is grounded in simple, immaterial substances called monads. Though they do not directly affect one another, God’s “pre-established harmony” makes their independent activity appear coordinated. In his 1710 Theodicy, Leibniz defended the religious-philosophical claim that God chose the best among possible worlds, addressing how evil could exist in such a world. He also developed calculus independently of Isaac Newton; Leibniz’s differential and integral notation helped shape the symbols still used in mathematics.\",\n    \"source_urls\": [\n      \"https://iep.utm.edu/leib-ove/\",\n      \"https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Leibniz/\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"key_facts\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"He was born in Leipzig on 1 July 1646 and died in Hannover on 14 November 1716.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://www.uni-hannover.de/en/universitaet/profil/leibniz/lebenslauf\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Leibniz’s monads were simple, immaterial substances that, in his theory, did not directly interact; their coordination was explained by pre-established harmony.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://iep.utm.edu/leib-ove/\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Published in 1710, his Theodicy defended the thesis that this is the best of all possible worlds and addressed the problem of evil.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://iep.utm.edu/leib-ove/\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"In 1714, he wrote the Monadology, a compact summary of his philosophical views.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://iep.utm.edu/leib-ove/\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Leibniz developed calculus independently of Newton and published his differential notation in 1684 and integral notation in 1686.\",\n      \"source_urls\": [\n        \"https://iep.utm.edu/leib-ove/\",\n        \"https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Leibniz/\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz (1646–1716)\",\n      \"url\": \"https://iep.utm.edu/leib-ove/\",\n      \"publisher\": \"Internet Encyclopedia of Philosophy\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T17:21:55.374262+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"Leibniz’s rationalist philosophy; monads and pre-established harmony; the Theodicy, best-of-all-worlds thesis, and problem of evil; Monadology; independent development of calculus.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Gottfried Wilhelm von Leibniz\",\n      \"url\": \"https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Leibniz/\",\n      \"publisher\": \"MacTutor History of Mathematics, University of St Andrews\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T17:21:55.374262+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"Biographical and mathematical context, including Leibniz’s calculus notation and its publication.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"The Life and Work of Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.uni-hannover.de/en/universitaet/profil/leibniz/lebenslauf\",\n      \"publisher\": \"Leibniz University Hannover\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-09-24T17:21:55.374262+00:00\",\n      \"supports\": \"Leibniz’s birth and death dates and locations.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"research_queries\": [\n    \"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz biography monads pre-established harmony calculus university\",\n    \"Leibniz Monadology Stanford Encyclopedia Philosophy calculus independent Newton biography\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Identity, key doctrines, dates, and calculus claims were checked against opened university, mathematics-history, and philosophy-encyclopedia pages. The best-of-all-worlds idea is presented as Leibniz’s defended philosophical and religious claim, not as an established fact.\",\n  \"unresolved_concerns\": [],\n  \"self_check_complete\": true\n}"
